  "scientific_adjudication": [
    "Same-partition CoRichards is fully available, so the Layer-ROM transfer findings are not confounded by comparator coverage.",
    "For five of six materials at L4, CoRichards is componentwise no worse on the six-component groundwater vector; B16 is the bounded exception where the simplified L4 route has a compensating GW advantage over coarse Richards.",
    "At higher dimension, CoRichards converges much more strongly toward Reference on B02, B11, B12 and B16 while Layer-ROM retains nonzero exchange/flux error. This is a model-form/closure signal, not evidence for missing vertical state alone.",
    "The B02 and B16 L6-to-R8 storage/cumulative-exchange reversals are Layer-ROM-specific: same-partition Richards remains monotone. Those reversals therefore should not drive a conclusion that more vertical states are intrinsically harmful.",
    "B05 remains intrinsically difficult at L4 for both routes, but Layer-ROM is substantially worse on every GW6 component. Both discretization and layer-closure/model-form contribute there.",
    "R8 B05 and B06 remain vector tradeoffs, so a claim that CoRichards is universally superior at every component would be false.",
    "Profile reconstruction error remains strongly tied to the shared coarse partition and must stay separate from groundwater-exchange fidelity."
  ],
